From 3c7e640a49d6cafda5eb053e5ea1d87ee2ef14d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexis Williams <alexis@typedr.at>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:36:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] spa: alsa: Follow external volume changes via Monitor

ACP opens a second connection for the streaming Monitor call and
applies the pushed volume and mute to the active route, so changes
made on the device itself show up in PipeWire.

If the service is unreachable when the card comes up, or goes away
later, both connections are retried on a 1 s timer. A replacement is
swapped in only once it connects, so calls fail meanwhile instead of
falling through to the card's own mixer. Capabilities learned on a
late connect install the devices' volume and mute hooks then. A
Monitor stream that ends is restarted, backing off up to 30 s while
the service keeps refusing it.
